// FAQ - Room Creation
"faq.roomCreation" = "Room Creation";
"faq.howToCreate" = "How do I create a 3D room?";
"faq.howToCreateAnswer" = "Tap Photo → 3D on the home screen (or Create Room from Photo when your room list is empty), then take or select a photo. Choose AI Room or Manual Setup to continue.";
"faq.howToTakePhoto" = "How do I take a photo to create a room?";
"faq.howToTakePhotoAnswer" = "When creating a room, choose Take a Photo. You can pick Standard (1x) or Wide Angle (0.5× ultra-wide). Hold your device steady and tap capture. The photo is then used to build your 3D room.";
"faq.twoMethods" = "What are the two room creation options?";
"faq.twoMethodsAnswer" = "AI Room automatically estimates room depth and dimensions from the photo. Manual Setup lets you draw the room boundaries yourself for more control.";
"faq.whatIsAIRoom" = "What is AI-Powered 3D Room?";
"faq.whatIsAIRoomAnswer" = "AI Room uses Depth Anything for metric depth, RTMDet furniture anchors, and GeoCalib for camera calibration. It builds a measured textured room from one photo without boundary drawing.";
"faq.whatIsManualRoom" = "What is Manual Setup?";
"faq.whatIsManualRoomAnswer" = "With Manual Setup, you draw the outline of your room's walls on the photo. This gives you more control over exactly how the 3D room looks. It's great when you want to fine-tune the room shape yourself.";
"faq.whichMethodBetter" = "Which method should I choose?";
"faq.whichMethodBetterAnswer" = "Try AI-Powered first - it's faster and works great for most rooms. If the result doesn't look quite right, use Manual Setup to draw the walls exactly where you want them. You can always try both and see which one you prefer!";
"faq.bestPhotos" = "What kind of photos work best?";
"faq.bestPhotosAnswer" = "For best results, take photos in good lighting with the camera held level. Try to capture the entire room including floors, walls, and ceiling edges. Avoid blurry or dark photos.";
"faq.generationFailing" = "Why is my room generation failing?";
"faq.generationFailingAnswer" = "Room generation may fail if the photo is too dark, blurry, or doesn't show enough room features. Try taking a new photo with better lighting and a wider angle.";
"faq.howManyRooms" = "How many rooms can I create?";
"faq.howManyRoomsAnswer" = "You can create up to 20 rooms. Delete older rooms to make space for new ones. The room count and total storage used are shown at the top of your home screen.";
"faq.howToSaveRoom" = "How do I save a room?";
"faq.howToSaveRoomAnswer" = "After generating a 3D room, tap the room to summon controls, then tap the save icon (download arrow) and enter a name. If you leave a preview without saving, that room is discarded.";
"faq.whereRoomsSaved" = "Where are my rooms saved?";
"faq.whereRoomsSavedAnswer" = "Rooms are stored locally in Paafekt's private app storage at Documents/SavedRooms. They are not uploaded automatically. Deleting the app also removes locally saved rooms, so explicitly share any room you need elsewhere.";
"faq.arePhotosUploaded" = "Are my room photos uploaded?";
"faq.arePhotosUploadedAnswer" = "Core room reconstruction, furniture detection, and Placement Intelligence run on device. Raw room photos are not uploaded for these features. Firebase processes account authentication data, and content leaves the device only when you explicitly share it.";

// FAQ - AI Features
"faq.aiFeatures" = "AI Features";
"faq.whatIsBrainIcon" = "What does the Fit button do?";
"faq.whatIsBrainIconAnswer" = "Tap the gold Fit button (bottom-right) in the room viewer to start SmartyPants furniture segmentation. By default it auto-segments the highest-confidence item as a transparent cutout over your 3D room. Tap Done (top-right) to exit. For tap-to-select specific pieces, summon controls and enable full-video mode first.";
"faq.whatIsViewfinderButton" = "What does full-video mode do in the room viewer?";
"faq.whatIsViewfinderButtonAnswer" = "While Fit is active, summon controls and tap the viewfinder icon to toggle full-video mode. You get a live camera feed with detection boxes—tap one or more items, then tap Segment. The camera hides and transparent cutouts composite over your 3D room. Tap Done (top-right) to exit segment mode or leave Fit entirely.";
"faq.howToScreenshot" = "How do I take a screenshot?";
"faq.howToScreenshotAnswer" = "Tap the room to summon controls, then tap Capture. This saves the current view (including furniture overlays when Fit is on) to your Photos library.";
"faq.whatIsSegmentation" = "What is furniture segmentation?";
"faq.whatIsSegmentationAnswer" = "Furniture segmentation runs from the room viewer via the Fit button. By default one primary item is auto-segmented. In full-video mode, select detected items first; Segment then creates transparent cutouts only for those pieces.";
"faq.howToSegment" = "How do I segment furniture in the room viewer?";
"faq.howToSegmentAnswer" = "Tap Fit in the room viewer. For a quick check it auto-segments the main item. To pick specific pieces: summon controls, enable full-video mode, point the camera at the furniture, tap detection boxes, then tap Segment. Tap Done (top-right) to exit.";
"faq.notDetected" = "Why isn't my furniture being detected?";
"faq.notDetectedAnswer" = "Object detection works best with clear, well-lit environments where furniture is clearly visible. Make sure the object isn't partially hidden or too far from the camera.";

// FAQ - 3D Room Controls
"faq.roomControls" = "3D Room Controls";
"faq.howToView" = "How do I view my 3D room?";
"faq.howToViewAnswer" = "Tap any room on the home screen to open the 3D viewer. Drag to look around and pinch to zoom. Tap the room to summon extra controls (recenter, ruler, Capture). The gold Fit button stays visible at bottom-right.";
"faq.howToNavigate" = "How do I navigate inside the room?";
"faq.howToNavigateAnswer" = "Drag on the room to orbit the camera and pinch to zoom. Tap the screen to summon the toolbar, then tap Recenter to restore the default view. The small control at bottom-left also brings the toolbar back when hidden.";
"faq.whatDoArrowsDo" = "How do I show or hide viewer controls?";
"faq.whatDoArrowsDoAnswer" = "The room viewer uses immersive mode—controls hide for a clean view. Tap the room to summon the toolbar. The gold Fit button at bottom-right is always visible. While Fit is active, Done appears top-right to exit segmentation.";
"faq.whatIsMemoryDisplay" = "What does the MB number mean?";
"faq.whatIsMemoryDisplayAnswer" = "The MB (megabytes) shown in rooms indicates the file size. This helps you manage storage. The total storage used by all rooms is shown at the top of the home screen.";
"faq.howToPlace" = "How do I place furniture in my room?";
"faq.howToPlaceAnswer" = "After you tap Segment, the selected furniture appears as an overlay in the room. Drag to position it and pinch to resize it.";
"faq.sampleRoom" = "Can I use a sample room instead of my own?";
"faq.sampleRoomAnswer" = "Yes! The app provides sample rooms (Scandinavian Minimal, Industrial Loft) for you to experiment with. Access them from the home screen to try out features without creating your own room first.";
"faq.accuracy" = "How accurate is the 3D model?";
"faq.accuracyAnswer" = "The 3D room is estimated from one photo using camera calibration and metric depth. Dimensions are useful as guidance, not tape-measure accurate. Furniture sizing is most reliable on phones with AR/depth support.";
"faq.adjustDimensions" = "Can I adjust room dimensions?";
"faq.adjustDimensionsAnswer" = "You cannot edit AI room dimensions manually. After saving, summon controls and tap the ruler to see estimated width, height, and depth. During the pre-save preview, dimension chips are hidden—save the room first, then reopen to see measurements. Manual rooms follow the boundaries you draw.";
"faq.furnitureMeasurements" = "Furniture & measurements";
"faq.arAssistedSizing" = "How is furniture overlay size estimated?";
"faq.arAssistedSizingAnswer" = "Tap Fit to segment furniture first. Use the sizing control in the summoned toolbar when you want room-relative scale. On phones with AR/depth support, the app uses live camera depth; without depth, furniture measurements are approximate.";
"faq.measurementPill" = "What is the small measurement readout?";
"faq.measurementPillAnswer" = "The furniture size pill appears only when sizing mode is on and the app has a usable live height estimate. The ruler button shows the current room width, height, and depth in a small card. On non-AR phones, these readings are less reliable, especially for furniture.";
"faq.resetOverlayScale" = "The furniture mask looks wrongly zoomed—what can I do?";
"faq.resetOverlayScaleAnswer" = "There is no overflow menu now. If the overlay looks off, tap Done to exit Fit and tap Fit again, or pinch the furniture manually to fine-tune its size.";
"faq.depthAwareRoomPhoto" = "Does taking a photo in the app help room quality?";
"faq.depthAwareRoomPhotoAnswer" = "Yes. On supported devices, choosing Take a photo (instead of picking from the gallery) uses the in-app camera with depth where available, which can improve how your 3D room is built and scaled.";
"faq.multiplePieces" = "Can I add multiple furniture pieces?";
"faq.multiplePiecesAnswer" = "Yes! In full-video mode you can tap several detection boxes, then tap Segment once to cut out all selected pieces together over your 3D room. You can also segment items one at a time using the default Fit flow.";
"faq.roomFitment" = "How do I check if furniture fits?";
"faq.roomFitmentAnswer" = "After segmentation, enable AR sizing for measured furniture width and height. Placement Intelligence compares those values and derived depth with the room envelope. It does not identify a guaranteed free floor location.";

// FAQ - Placement intelligence & aesthetic
"faq.placementIntelligence" = "Placement intelligence & aesthetic";
"faq.whatIsPlacementIntelligence" = "What is Placement Intelligence?";
"faq.whatIsPlacementIntelligenceAnswer" = "While Fit is active, Placement Intelligence compares AR-measured furniture width and height, plus derived depth, with the room envelope. It reports dimensional fit rather than claiming a free placement location. Tap the header to expand details.";
"faq.furnitureColorAesthetic" = "How does the app pick a color for aesthetic scoring?";
"faq.furnitureColorAestheticAnswer" = "The app averages the straight RGB color of visible pixels inside the AI furniture cutout and compares it with colors sampled from the room. If either sample is unavailable, aesthetic guidance remains unavailable instead of inventing a score.";
"faq.whatDoHarmonyContrastMean" = "What do harmony, contrast, and style fit mean?";
"faq.whatDoHarmonyContrastMeanAnswer" = "These are simple design heuristics, not a judgment of taste. Harmony describes how the furniture color relates to the room palette (for example analogous or complementary hues). Contrast is how different the brightness is from typical floor or wall colors. Style fit compares broad style labels inferred for the room with a default modern profile, so it is approximate.";
"faq.whenDoesAestheticScoreLow" = "When might aesthetic scores look low or show \"clash\"?";
"faq.whenDoesAestheticScoreLowAnswer" = "Bright, saturated objects often score worse when their hue does not line up with the app's harmonious color schemes against your room—for example acid green, magenta, purple, or safety-orange props against warm beige or tan rooms, or loud primaries in a room sampled as mostly one hue family. Very similar brightness to the floor or wall (brown-on-brown, gray-on-gray) can lower contrast even if you like the look. Rooms inferred as rustic or traditional can show lower style fit because the furniture profile uses default modern/minimal tags. Dull gray or muddy averages from busy backgrounds may land in a neutral band instead of clash. Treat scores as guides only and trust your eye for real decor.";

